## Key Concepts
- Per-core buffering and cross-core publication
- Sequence-numbered slots and wrap-around handling
- Memory ordering on x86-64 (relaxed/upholds with fences)
- False sharing avoidance and cacheline padding
- Validation: throughput, ordering, and backpressure under contention

## Code Example
```c
// Pseudo-enqueue
bool enqueue(int core_id, void* msg) {
  uint64_t pos = atomic_fetch_add(&tail[core_id], 1);
  slot_t* s = &ring[core_id][pos & (N-1)];
  if (s->seq != pos) return false; // consumer hasn't advanced
  s->payload = msg;
  s->seq = pos + 1;
  return true;
}
```

